From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:15:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/runtime: refuse a pipeline create info that names no
 pipeline

vkGetPipelineKeyKHR, and vkCreatePipelineBinariesKHR where the driver has an
internal cache to look a pipeline up in, take the pipeline from the first
structure of the chain of a VkPipelineCreateInfoKHR, and read it as the
create info of a graphics, compute or ray tracing pipeline by its type. The
chain is the application's and the generated validation does not require it,
so a create info with no chain reached a read of a null pointer, and one that
begins with another structure ended in UNREACHABLE: in a release build the
switch then fell into a case that reads the structure with the layout of a
graphics pipeline's, taking its stage count and stage array from fields the
application chose and reading past the end of the structure.

Both commands now return VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED, a result each defines
and the one the implementation gives when it detects invalid usage, for an
empty chain and for a first structure that names no pipeline. The key of the
device itself, a create info of NULL, is served as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
index 2fd9d8426c8a7660f1284a97da65993a675a3f33..0a3eac7238e78bf15c711b979c98d6f5ba2774ce 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
@@ -4288,6 +4288,13 @@ vk_common_CreatePipelineBinariesKHR(
       struct vk_pipeline_cache *cache = device->mem_cache;
       const VkBaseInStructure *next = pCreateInfo->pPipelineCreateInfo->pNext;
 
+      /* The pipeline create info names its pipeline in the structure that
+       * begins its chain (see vk_common_GetPipelineKeyKHR). */
+      if (next == NULL) {
+         return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED,
+                          "a pipeline create info has an empty chain");
+      }
+
       switch (next->sType) {
       case VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_GRAPHICS_PIPELINE_CREATE_INFO: {
          struct vk_graphics_pipeline_state state_tmp;
@@ -4405,7 +4412,9 @@ vk_common_CreatePipelineBinariesKHR(
       }
 
       default:
-         UNREACHABLE("Unsupported pNext");
+         return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED,
+                          "a pipeline create info begins with structure type "
+                          "%d, not a pipeline's", next->sType);
       }
    } else if (pipeline != NULL) {
       switch (pipeline->bind_point) {
@@ -4569,7 +4578,20 @@ vk_common_GetPipelineKeyKHR(
       return VK_SUCCESS;
    }
 
+   /* A pipeline create info names its pipeline in the structure that begins
+    * its chain: the graphics, compute or ray tracing pipeline create info
+    * read below.  The chain is the application's, and the generated
+    * validation does not require it, so a create info with no chain, or with
+    * another structure first, names no pipeline to key.  Reading that
+    * structure as a pipeline's would take its fields from another type's
+    * layout, so it is refused instead.  VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED is the
+    * result a command gives when the implementation detects invalid usage,
+    * and this command defines it. */
    const VkBaseInStructure *next = pPipelineCreateInfo->pNext;
+   if (next == NULL) {
+      return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED,
+                       "a pipeline create info has an empty chain");
+   }
 
    struct mesa_blake3 blake3_ctx;
    _mesa_blake3_init(&blake3_ctx);
@@ -4626,7 +4648,9 @@ vk_common_GetPipelineKeyKHR(
    }
 
    default:
-      UNREACHABLE("Unsupported pNext");
+      return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED,
+                       "a pipeline create info begins with structure type %d, "
+                       "not a pipeline's", next->sType);
    }
 
    pPipelineKey->keySize = sizeof(blake3_hash);
